  "id": "COMPOUND:27192 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Fumotonaringin is implicated in the targeting of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is a key component of the cellular redox system. This targeting is mediated by multiple compounds, including (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver and 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, all of which have been shown to target A549 cells. The integration of these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which Fumotonaringin may exert its effects on A549 cells, possibly through the modulation of mitochondrial thioredoxin, which is involved in cellular stress responses and apoptosis. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with A549 cells indicates a possible role in cellular dysfunction or death, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a link between Fumotonaringin and A549 through a pathway involving thioredoxin, but further investigation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the precise molecular mechanism.",
